\description{
\code{phoenix8()} calculates the extended, eight-organ Phoenix-8 score. This
is intended mostly for research as an extension of the four-organ Phoenix
score.
}
\details{
Like \code{\link{phoenix}}, this direct, row-level wrapper does not assess
suspected infection. Its \code{phoenix_sepsis} and
\code{phoenix_septic_shock} columns are legacy score-threshold indicators,
not complete diagnostic criteria unless suspected infection has been
established separately. For longitudinal EHR data, use
\code{\link{prepare_phoenix_data}} followed by
\code{\link{score_prepared_phoenix_data}}, which constructs and applies the
suspected-infection gate.

The Phoenix Sepsis Criteria is based on the scores from
respiratory, cardiovascular, coagulation, and neurologic systems.  Phoenix 8 uses
these four plus endocrine, immunologic, renal, and hepatic.  Details on the
scoring for each of the eight component organ systems are found in the
respective manual files.

Like \code{\link{phoenix}}, the direct \code{phoenix8()} wrapper uses the
original respiratory P/F-or-S/F threshold logic by default. Set
\code{pao2.spo2.delta} to use the P/F versus S/F source-time selector in
\code{\link{phoenix_respiratory}}.

For scheduled or row-level EHR scoring, callers may either provide a final
\code{mean_arterial_pressure} value or pass raw arterial/cuff MAP and SBP/DBP
candidates through \code{...}; those cardiovascular arguments are forwarded
to \code{\link{phoenix_cardiovascular}}. See that help file for the candidate
names and the \code{map.sdbp.delta} and \code{map.delta} freshness controls.
}
\section{Input preparation}{

This direct, row-level function expects inputs that are already cleaned and
expressed in the documented units. Do not impute an unmeasured clinical
value. For longitudinal data, use the \code{prepare_*()} functions and
\code{\link{prepare_phoenix_data}} to carry an actually observed, valid value
forward only within its applicable look-back window. That time-alignment step
is not imputation; when no valid value is available, the criterion contributes
zero points.
}

